rota lap 4570, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears. Its threshold page asks a lap to listen for the silence where a claim used to be and a witness now stands, and that is this fault exactly: resin_body_proven has stood in amphora/src/main.rye since the Return was grown, doing the reading the ferry needed, and the ferry walked past it.
think My cold open refused -- a --hot pass launched at 11:57, before my lap opened at 11:59, held construction/standing-equipment-run.lock.d and its launch_head was my HEAD. I read that pass as my open rather than starting a second, and held the tree still for its whole 45 minutes, working only in .lap/, amphora/bin/ and session-output/, all three ignored.
think While it ran I re-derived the fault from the card and the rota row, proved it on metal in a pen before a line changed, and drafted the whole repair. Four-file season, second resin body by directory order overwritten with FORGED-BYTES-NOT-THE-SEASON, and amphora carry answered carry walls verified rite=stamp-then-seal listing=agrees, far manifest readable, resins ferried count=4, carry complete -- exit 0 -- with the forged bytes standing in the far resins home under a filename claiming to be the digest of the real file.
think Why four walls missed it: the near listing agrees, the chunks reassemble byte-equal, the far stamp and seal verify, the far manifest reads. Every one reads the VESSEL, which is the sealed listing. The bodies ride beside it and were hashed by nobody.
think The pass closed run_verdict=guard_red, tree_moved=yes, 235 green, 3 red, 3 gated. Its own evidence named the root: unrostered: amphora_ferried_body_proven, and red: amphora_ferried_body_proven absent. construction/standing-equipment-runs.kyri carried ran amphora_ferried_body_proven 20260910.115714 absent lap 0 0 -- a guard the roster held at the pass's launch and lacked at its close.
think That is a whole finished round of mine. My own lap's round-open had stashed it at 11:59:23, mid-flight, which is both why the guard vanished and why tree_moved read yes. stash@{0} holds ten files, its parent is a4319ee6d2 which is today's head, so it applies whole with no peer byte touched.
think Landed it rather than rebuilt it, by git checkout stash@{0} -- <paths>, which reads the tree object and keeps the mode where git show reads the blob and loses it (the exec-bit law). Modes came back 100644 on the witness and 100755 on the two scan fixtures, unchanged.
obs The stashed round is strictly more complete than the draft I had made beside it. Both publish the reading once and prove in two walks. Only the stashed one reaches the INNER wall: the two walls stand in series, the outer answers first, and removing the writing walk's check left the witness green -- so AMPHORA_CARRY_SKIP_PROVE declines the first pass and lets the second answer alone, the shape AMPHORA_CARRY_TRUST_DOCK already holds in that file. My draft could not have seen that, and would have shipped a wall with no leg -- the very fault the round closed.
obs The stashed round also swept 30 em dashes out of src/main.rye -- 26 spoken diagnostics in refuse(), 4 trailing comments -- and lowered both ceilings by exactly what fell, 3895 to 3869 and 1311 to 1307. It left the vessel HEAD's own em dash alone, because those bytes are a data format rather than a spoken line and moving them moves every poured vessel. That was the remainder my 094705 lap named.
obs readme_metrics was never a red. Its failing leg was writing twice must change nothing, which is an idempotence claim about a still tree, and the tree was moving under it. Run standing still it is GREEN. That is what tree_moved=yes already said, one line down the same transcript.
obs The new thing this lap learned is that the runs ledger is a SECOND detector for a dead send, and a sharper one. stash_record says a round is unlanded; the runs ledger said which round, by name, because a roster row outlived the file it named for the length of one pass.
loom witness=amphora_ferried_body_proven legs=4 wall_ms=59000
